# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch A."""
DESC_A = {
    "KW": {
        14: """Gendarme is a dome city on the Moon that serves as the capital of the Moonrace's living sphere. It was built by the Ghingnham family, who continue to serve as the city's guardians.
The palace of Queen Dianna Soreil, the 'White Palace,' and the 'Winter Palace,' a facility for the cryogenic hibernation of countless citizens, are also located here.""",
        15: """An autonomous city in the northern part of the North American continent, governed by Mayor Nomoa Long. It is protected by a civilian defense force centered on Carris Nautilus, an artificial Newtype created by Nomoa.
In truth, Nomoa was Dr. Dorat of the Space Revolutionary Army in disguise, and Fort Severn was built as a cover to restore the giant Newtype-exclusive mobile armor Patulia, in order to complete 'Operation Lilac,' a plan that had been foiled by the Federation forces during the Seventh Space War. Nomoa activated Patulia with Carris as its pilot, but his ambitions were destroyed along with him thanks to Freeden's efforts and Carris's resolve.
Afterward, the city was rebuilt around Carris and given a fresh start as a truly autonomous city.
Incidentally, a real city of the same name exists in Canada.""",
        16: """A term for human beings born naturally, without genetic adjustment. The designation came into use after the emergence of Coordinators, humans whose genes had been adjusted.
Many Naturals feel jealousy or hostility toward Coordinators, who possess superior abilities. At the same time, no small number of Coordinators look down on Naturals, flaunting their gifts. As a result, some Naturals openly advocate opposition to Coordinators, the foremost of whom are Blue Cosmos.""",
        17: """A general term for human beings whose genes were adjusted at the fertilized egg stage to grant them heightened intelligence and a robust body. Their existence became known to the world in C.E. 15, when George Glenn, the First Coordinator, made a worldwide confession broadcast.
Coordinators are born with many superior traits, both physical and mental. However, whether or not those abilities blossom depends heavily on the environment in which they are raised.
Most Coordinators live on the PLANTs, though there are exceptional places, such as the neutral nation of Orb or lunar cities, where they coexist with Naturals (ordinary humans who have not undergone genetic adjustment).
Those born to Natural parents through genetic adjustment are called 'First-Generation Coordinators,' while children born between two Coordinators are called 'Second-Generation Coordinators.' However, the birth rate has been declining year by year, and this has become a major social problem.""",
        18: """A political organization known for its extremism. All of its members are Naturals, and under the slogan "For a Pure and Blue World," it seeks the eradication of Coordinators. Even among Naturals who have not joined Blue Cosmos, many regard Coordinators with suspicion - a result of the organization's manipulation of public opinion.
However, the political front is only a facade. Behind the scenes, Blue Cosmos hides its true nature as a secret society acting as the hands and feet of LOGOS in pursuit of the total eradication of Coordinators. This is possible because its members have infiltrated deep into the core of the Earth Alliance and the Earth Alliance Forces.
After its leader Muruta Azrael died in the Second Battle of Jachin Due in C.E. 71, the organization kept a low profile for a time. But once Lord Djibril took over as its new leader, it once again began manipulating public opinion through the Atlantic Federation and the media, working to drag the Earth Alliance and the PLANTs back into war.""",
        19: """A military-industrial complex said to have existed since the dawn of recorded history, wielding powerful influence over politics. It is made up of merchants of death who have secretly manipulated wars and postwar reconstruction alike to reap enormous profits.
LOGOS is the backer of Blue Cosmos and has guided public opinion to provoke war between the Earth Alliance and the Coordinators. Both Muruta Azrael, Blue Cosmos's former leader, and Lord Djibril, its current leader, are members of LOGOS. For LOGOS, the true goal is to keep profiting by continuing the war; the fact that Blue Cosmos champions the eradication of Coordinators owes much to the personal feelings of these two men.
Since it possesses no military force of its own, LOGOS moved the Earth Alliance Forces to attempt to annihilate the Coordinators during the previous war. After the war, it organized Phantom Pain to wield power more directly.""",
        20: """A term referring to the new generation of space colonies inhabited by Coordinators, their collective grouping, and the Coordinator nation itself. The name is an abbreviation for 'Production Location Ally on Nexus Technology,' and it doubles as a reference to a 'large-scale production base.'
As a nation, the PLANTs are administered by the PLANT Supreme Council. In the past, the Earth Alliance sought to prevent the PLANTs' autonomy and independence by imposing heavy taxes and pressure on them, which became one of the triggers of the previous war.
As a residential zone, the PLANTs are concentrated at L5, one of the Lagrange points where Earth's and the Moon's gravity balance.""",
        21: """The highest authority of the PLANT Supreme Council, the PLANTs' foremost decision-making body. Since the signing of the Junius Treaty, Gilbert Durandal has held the post.
Patrick Zala once held this post concurrently with that of Chairman of National Defense, and it was his hatred and madness that dragged the war into a quagmire. In reflection of that, holding both posts simultaneously is forbidden today.""",
        22: """A special unit of ZAFT, its name an abbreviation for 'Fast Acting Integrated Tactical Headquarters.'
Only those whose character and combat record are recognized as truly exceptional are admitted, with the approval of both the Chairman of National Defense and the Chairman of the PLANT Council. Members are given a silver badge as proof of their status, and its bearers always command the respect and envy of those around them.
Despite being called a special unit, its members do not belong to any single unit; they are permitted to act and give orders based on their own judgment. Their authority is considerable, extending even to giving orders to field commanders.""",
        23: """Chairman of National Defense on the PLANT Supreme Council during the previous war. Athrun's father.
He lost his wife in the Earth Alliance's surprise attack on Junius Seven, the incident that triggered the previous war. This filled him with intense hatred for Naturals, and he advocated all-out resistance against the Earth Alliance. He later drove out the moderate former PLANT Council Chairman Siegel Clyne and his faction, seizing the chairmanship for himself.
In the Second Battle of Jachin Due, he attempted to annihilate the Naturals with the 'GENESIS,' an enormous gamma-ray laser cannon capable of devastating Earth's environment, but was shot dead by an aide who feared for the PLANTs' future.""",
        24: """The PLANTs' military organization, its name an abbreviation for 'Zodiac Alliance of Freedom Treaty.'
Its roots lie in a political society formed chiefly by Siegel Clyne and Patrick Zala, and it is made up of volunteer soldiers drawn from the Coordinator populace. All members are trained to fight on land, at sea, and in the air without distinction, and the most outstanding soldiers are granted the uniform known as the 'Red Coat.'
ZAFT has no ranks like those of a conventional military; instead, units are named directly after their commanders. Supreme command authority rests with the Chairman of National Defense of the PLANT Council.""",
        25: """A military PLANT held by ZAFT in the L4 region.
It was developing the 'Second Stage' mobile suits, represented by the Impulse, as well as the new-model warship Minerva that operates them.""",
        26: """The capital of the PLANTs, located in the L5 region.""",
        27: """An international body established primarily by nations opposed to the PLANTs and by former PLANT-affiliated member states.
After the previous war ended, under the leadership of the Atlantic Federation - its strongest military power - the Earth Alliance used the Earth Alliance Forces to militarily annex pro-PLANT nations one after another. Only a handful of nations, such as the Orb Union and the Kingdom of Scandinavia, remained unaffiliated and neutral.
Triggered by 'Break the World,' the incident in which Coordinators caused Junius Seven to fall to Earth, the Earth Alliance once again marched down the road to war with the PLANTs. Behind the scenes, it appears Blue Cosmos and LOGOS were involved.""",
        28: """The Orb Union. A small nation in the Pacific Ocean made up of several islands.
It is a rare place where Naturals and Coordinators coexist peacefully, and it has declared a neutral stance, siding with neither the Earth Alliance nor ZAFT. It is home to the state-run Morgenroete Inc.
Orb declared neutrality during the previous war as well, but its land was scorched by war when the Earth Alliance invaded. Though its infrastructure has since been rebuilt, the loss of many talented people as a result of the war remains a headache for its current chief representative, Cagalli Yula Athha.
Despite her title, the young Cagalli finds it difficult to seize the initiative, and within the government the ambitions of the Five Great Clans that guide the nation are in constant conflict. Chief among them is Unato, head of the Seiran family and serving as prime minister, whose lust for power drives him to scheme to marry his son Yuna to Cagalli in order to seize control of the nation's government.""",
        29: """Uzumi Nara Athha. The chief representative of Orb two generations before the present, and adoptive father of the current chief representative, Cagalli Yula Athha.
A shrewd and capable politician known as the 'Lion of Orb' for his resolute manner and uncompromising integrity.
During the previous war, he tried to maintain neutrality, submitting to neither the Earth Alliance nor ZAFT. But the Earth Alliance launched an invasion to annex Orb and seize its mass driver.
Though he resisted to the very end, the tide of battle turned decisively against him. Entrusting the future to Cagalli and the Archangel, he evacuated the citizens and then destroyed both the mass driver and Morgenroete Inc. by his own hand, sharing the fate of his burning nation.""",
        30: """A state-run company of the Orb Union with a dock on Onogoro Island. During the previous war, it developed the 'G' series of mobile suits, including the Strike and the Aegis.
Its technological prowess rivals that of ZAFT, as shown by its development of the 'Murasame,' the variable-type mass-production mobile suit that serves as the mainstay of Orb's forces.
It also has deep ties to the Archangel, which it once helped develop, and it secretly carries out the ship's refits and resupply.""",
        31: """A term for the fighting during the previous war that began with the Earth Alliance's invasion of Orb.
Seeking to seize the 'Kaguya,' the mass driver (a large-scale mass-projection device) essential for contesting ZAFT's control of space, the Earth Alliance deployed its new 'GAT-X' series mobile suits. Orb's forces met them with the secretly developed mass-production mobile suit 'M1 Astray,' but were ultimately forced into defeat by overwhelming numbers.
The Archangel, having broken away from the military, also joined the defense, but was forced to withdraw from the battle line after Uzumi entrusted it with the world's future.
This two-day battle came to an end when Uzumi vanished into the flames along with a key facility.""",
        32: """A term for the battle fought in the final stage of the previous war, in the region of Jachin Due, ZAFT's space fortress. Many officers and soldiers on both sides, including Mwu La Flaga, Muruta Azrael, and Patrick Zala, were killed or went missing.
In this battle, the 'GENESIS,' ZAFT's ultimate weapon - an enormous gamma-ray laser cannon - was fired twice, and the Earth Alliance Forces lost more than 40 percent of their space fleet along with the Ptolemaeus base on the Moon.
The First Battle of Jachin Due, meanwhile, refers to the fighting that broke out between the Earth Alliance Forces and ZAFT immediately after the outbreak of war, when the Alliance attempted to strike the PLANT homeland. This battle was the catalyst for converting Jachin Due, then still only a resource satellite, into a space fortress.""",
        33: """Rau Le Creuset. A capable ZAFT commander. In truth he was a Natural, but he concealed this fact when he enlisted with ZAFT.
He was born as a clone of Al Da Flaga, Mwu's father, but because his telomeres, which govern lifespan, were shorter than those of an ordinary person, he was treated as a defective product.
Learning this truth, he came to hate the very world that had produced a being like himself. He eventually leaked operational details and handed over military secrets in an attempt to bring about the mutual destruction of both ZAFT and the Alliance. As a result, his scheme had very nearly succeeded by the time of the Second Battle of Jachin Due. However, he was defeated in battle against the Freedom, and vanished cursing the world into the light of the runaway GENESIS.
Perhaps because of a special drug he took regularly to slow his aging, he was occasionally seen suffering from side effects. It is thought that he always hid his face behind a mask to conceal features aged beyond his years, along with the dark ambition he kept hidden within.""",
        34: """A wartime treaty concluded between the Earth Alliance and the PLANTs on March 10, C.E. 72, the year after the previous war ended. It takes its name from the fact that it was signed at Junius Seven, where the scars of the previous war still ran deep.
Its main purpose was to limit armaments, establishing an upper limit on the number of mobile suits each side could hold and banning the use of Neutron Jammer Cancellers.
It also included provisions for restoring national borders, and nations such as the Orb Union, which had been annexed by the Earth Alliance during the war, regained their independence.""",
        35: """Enhanced humans developed by the Earth Alliance under Blue Cosmos's direction. They were deployed on the mission to seize the 'Second Stage Series' at Armory One.
They resolved the emotional instability that plagued the earlier generation of enhanced humans, the 'Biological CPUs,' successfully retaining the ability to fight Coordinators on equal or superior terms while also gaining enough cooperative capacity to work as a team.
However, if an Extended hears the Block Word set as a safety measure, they fall into an extremely unstable mental state.
Additionally, maintenance using an adjustment device called a 'cradle' is essential for them after combat.""",
        36: """A mental restraint imposed on the Extended, the enhanced humans developed by the Earth Alliance.
Though the Extended are more mentally stable than earlier generations of enhanced humans, hearing the assigned word instantly throws them into confusion and robs them of the ability to act calmly. Although it was set as a kind of safety mechanism, it carries numerous problems, including the risk of an Extended going berserk simply by speaking the word themselves.""",
        37: """The fossil of a gigantic creature with a bizarre shape that can only be described as "a whale with wings."
It was discovered by George Glenn, the First Coordinator, in a meteorite near Europa during a visit to Jupiter, and it is currently kept in the PLANT homeland.
It is said to be evidence of extraterrestrial life, but no new evidence has been found to support this theory.""",
        38: """Leaving one's current Dome Polis to escape to a region with a milder climate.
In the story, humanity is forced to live in Dome Polis, a collection of city units set up in harsh environments, ostensibly to protect the environment. But many of the People (as Dome Polis citizens are called) sense that this is merely a pretext used by the Siberian Railway, which holds a monopoly on the procurement of supplies, to pursue its own profit. As a result, People who dream of living somewhere better and carry out an Exodus are never in short supply.
However, Exodus is banned by the Siberian Railway and is treated as a serious crime that can be punished by death in the worst cases. Because of this, there exists a profession known as Exodus contractors, who smuggle people past the eyes of the Siberian Railway Security Force to their destination.""",
        39: """The sole transportation network across the land of Siberia. It is managed and operated by the Siberian Railway Corporation (commonly known as the Sibetetsu), headed by President Kids Mondo. Its headquarters are located in Liman Megalopolis.
Because it supplies the resources, food, and other lifelines that the Dome Polises along its lines depend on, the Siberian Railway is, in effect, the ruler of the Dome Polises.
Under its umbrella is the infamous armed organization known as the Siberian Railway Security Force. It also maintains close ties with the international monitoring body known as 'London IMA.'""",
        40: """A 3D fighting game in which players pilot Overmen to battle one another. Multiple players can compete simultaneously online.
At the start of the story, Gainer achieves 200 consecutive wins and earns the title of King.""",
        41: """Large garments literally worn by Overmen.
Wearing an Overcoat increases the power of Over Skills, or allows the wearer to acquire new Over Skills.
Each Overcoat is dedicated equipment for a specific Overman, but another Overman can also wear the coat and use the Over Skill hidden within it.""",
        42: """Rock formations that rise up in scab-like (scub) layers. They were given this name because their colorful appearance resembles coral. They are sometimes simply called Scub.
Because they can occur anywhere, human settlements drive massive stakes called 'pile bunkers' deep into the ground to prevent the formations from rising.
Buried beneath the Scub Coral are the archetypes of LFOs and KLFs. Because of this, many excavators are said to keep digging deep underground in search of them.""",
        43: """An abbreviation for 'Transparent Light Particle.' Trapar refers to mysterious, invisible particles that erupt from Scub Coral and drift through the air. Sky Fish, creatures of unknown origin, gather at points where Trapar is dense.
Trapar is used as an energy source in power plants and has already become indispensable to people's lives. Lift boards are able to fly by reflecting these particles.
But Trapar is not merely convenient; it can also turn against humanity. In the past, a phenomenon known as the Summer of Love, in which Trapar erupted abnormally, drove the world to the brink of destruction. It was the hero Adroc Thurston who saved the world from that crisis.""",
        44: """A worldwide phenomenon in which Trapar erupted abnormally. Many lives were lost.
This phenomenon is said to have been stopped at the cost of his life by Adroc Thurston, Renton's father. However, the details remain shrouded in mystery.""",
        45: """A sport in which riders use a lift board fitted with a wheel to ride the waves of Trapar drifting through the air. It is not limited to humans - even LFOs and KLFs can Ref if they use a suitably large lift board.
Its defining feature is the ability to pull off three-dimensional tricks unlike anything possible on a skateboard or surfboard. Many are captivated by the green trails drawn across the sky, and Ref is quite a major pastime within the world of the story. Those who Ref are called lift boarders.
Incidentally, a lift board is able to fly because a reflection film that reflects Trapar is attached to its underside.""",
        46: """A part attached to the underside of a lift board for balance control. The larger the wheel, the slower the speed, but the easier it becomes to pull off tricks.
Besides the wheel, many other factors determine a lift board's individuality, including its length and shape, and the form of the Trapar intake used to catch the waves of Trapar.""",
        47: """A special forces unit of the Tower State Federation Forces. It officially operates the blue-painted Terminus type R505. Holland, Eureka, Charles, and Ray all once served in its ranks.
SOF was also involved in the massacre of Vodarac believers at their holy site, an incident that became the catalyst for Holland's desertion from the military.""",
        48: """A religion whose teachings center on living in harmony with the Scub Coral.
Because of terrorism carried out by some of its more radical members, the Tower State Federation marks it as an anti-government organization. The general public's view is not far off, either; anyone found to be a believer is instantly regarded with suspicion.
Ciudad del Cielo, the faith's holy site, was once a beautiful town celebrated as a city in the sky. But it was utterly destroyed in the SOF massacre, and today lies in ruins.""",
        49: """An extremely popular accessory brand.
Talho is a huge fan, so much so that she badgered Holland into buying her a reissued silver ring. The ring was later crushed in a subsequent battle, but the incident ultimately strengthened the bond between the two of them.""",
        50: """An abbreviation for 'Universal Network.'
It is commonly pronounced 'U.N.'
An information network established by the New Earth Federation with the aim of centralizing and sharing information across the many parallel worlds.
Anyone with a terminal can browse or post information. In major metropolitan areas, it is not unusual for a connection to reach every household, but the further one gets from urban centers, the lower the rate of adoption becomes.
It serves as both a valuable source of information for citizens and an entertainment medium, making it an extremely important piece of infrastructure across the many parallel worlds.""",
        51: """A tactical research unit belonging to the Earth Federation Forces' lunar garrison.
It was formed for the purpose of evaluation testing and shakedown of new-model units, and its members possess exceptional piloting skills.
Its current mission is testing next-generation standard-issue production units and their onboard armaments, as well as researching applied combat tactics.""",
    },
    "RT": {
        0: """A super robot designed and developed by Dr. Juzo Kabuto.
It is completed when Kouji's Hover Pilder, launched from a sewage treatment plant with the shout "Mazin Go!", combines with the head (Pilder On).
It runs on photon power, and boasts a jumping ability of 20 meters, a grip strength of 150 tons, and 650,000 horsepower. Its armor, covered in Chogokin Z, is extremely sturdy, and ordinary attacks cannot leave so much as a scratch on it.
It carries a variety of weapons, including the 'Rocket Punch,' which fires its arms via rocket propulsion, the 'Breast Fire,' which emits thermal energy from its chest plate, and the 'Rust Hurricane,' which blasts a powerful acid-laden wind from its mouth. But its arsenal did not stop there - Professor Yumi and his colleagues went on to add new weapons and enhance its performance again and again.
Among its many upgrades, the most famous is the episode in which it overcame its greatest weakness, its inability to fly, thanks to the 'Jet Scrander' flight-assist device. This sequence of 'gaining wings and flying freely through the sky' embodies a longing humanity has held since the age of myth, and it left an extremely strong impression. As a result, many robot anime since have followed in its footsteps in one form or another.""",
        1: """A female-form robot developed by Professor Yumi to serve as Mazinger Z's partner.
It is the successor to the Aphrodite A, which was destroyed in battle against a Mechanical Beast, and it is completed when the large motorcycle 'Scarlet Mobile,' piloted by Sayaka, combines with its head. However, unlike the Aphrodite A, which was originally built for resource mining, Diana A was designed for combat from the outset, giving it considerably improved combat capability by comparison.
With photon power as its energy source, Chogokin Z armor, and a combining-type cockpit, it shares much in common with Mazinger Z, making it a robot truly worthy of the name 'partner.'""",
        2: """A super robot secretly designed and developed by Dr. Kenzo Kabuto, based on Mazinger Z.
Like Mazinger Z, it is completed when Tetsuya's Brain Condor, launched from a whirlpool with the shout "Mazin Go!", combines with the head (Fire On).
It runs on the same photon power as Mazinger Z, but its armor, made of Chogokin New Z, surpasses Chogokin Z and is even sturdier than Mazinger Z's.
Owing to the circumstances of its development, many of its weapons are enhanced or developed versions of those found on Mazinger Z. Its unique attacks include the 'Mazinger Blade,' a pair of giant swords stored in its legs, and 'Thunder Break,' which stores lightning as energy before unleashing it in a strike.
It also has the Scramble Dash flight device built into its back, allowing it to fly at Mach 4. Later, the 'Great Booster' was completed, a unit that combines with it to enhance its flight performance. This booster also doubled as a powerful weapon, unleashing destructive force comparable to a hydrogen bomb when rammed into an enemy.""",
        3: """A female-form combat robot developed to support Great Mazinger.
It is completed when Jun's small jet, the 'Quinstar,' launched from a waterfall basin, combines with its head.
Its overall combat power falls short of Great Mazinger's, but it carries weapons capable of standing up to the Battle Beasts, including the 'Photon Beam' fired from both eyes, the 'Finger Missile' launched from its fingertips, and the rapid-fire 'Photon Missile' from its chest.
It initially had no flight capability, but this was later remedied by the development of the Venus Scrander.""",
        4: """A giant robot built by the three doctors of the Photon Lab after Boss pressured them into it.
Perhaps because it was built from scrap, it seems to be extremely fragile, and it is beaten to pieces almost every time it fights. But it also seems easy to repair for the same reason, and it was operated solely by Boss and his two friends. Notably, only its head was built to be sturdy, and it never broke no matter what happened to it.
After helping Mazinger Z destroy Dr. Hell's forces, it joined Great Mazinger in standing against the ambitions of the Mycenae Empire.
At first it fought using nothing but the raw strength that had let it hold its own against Mechanical Beasts, but this proved useless against the Battle Beasts. To compensate, Boss and his friends developed a variety of weapons and finishing moves through trial and error, contributing to the fight with attacks such as the 'Drill Pressure Punch,' built for them by the American-trained Dr. Tobita, as well as the 'Boroboro Kick' and the 'Borot Spin Kick.'
Boss Borot is also the only robot to appear in all three of the original TV series. It even had a spin-off manga serialized in a children's magazine, leaving no doubt that it made a memorable impression in a very different way from the lead robots.""",
        5: """The form Grendizer takes when combined with its dedicated saucer-shaped mecha. The saucer-shaped mecha alone is also called the Spazer.
It supports Grendizer, which has no flight capability of its own; once combined, the pair can fly within the atmosphere at up to Mach 9 and travel between stars via hyperspace navigation. Like Grendizer, it runs on photon quantum energy and is armored in space alloy Guren.
Although some of Grendizer's own weapons become unusable, the Spazer's various built-in armaments were well suited to taking on large numbers of Minifors at once.
The enemy later discovered that combining with the Spazer took six seconds, and began targeting that window of vulnerability. This crisis was overcome by combining instead with three Earth-made Spazers developed by Dr. Umon, but as a result, the original Spazer saw dramatically less use in battle afterward.""",
        6: """A super robot developed as the guardian deity of Planet Fleed.
It runs on photon quantum energy, which is dispersed throughout the cosmos, and is protected by sturdy armor made of space alloy Guren. To prevent misuse by others, it is equipped with a self-defense system that unleashes an electric shock against anyone who tries to board it without the ring that marks the Fleed royal bloodline.
Its main weapons include the 'Double Harken,' which combines the crescent-shaped blades on both shoulders, and 'Space Thunder,' which fires energy generated from the horns on its head as an incandescent beam; combined with its 1.8 million horsepower, these give it extremely high combat capability.
It is powerful even alone, but combining with the dedicated saucer mecha known as the Spazer reinforces its aerial combat capability and interstellar travel range. However, the enemy discovered that combining with the Spazer took six seconds, and began targeting that window of vulnerability. This crisis was overcome by combining instead with three Earth-made Spazers developed by Dr. Umon, granting it even greater mobility and combat capability.""",
        7: """A small saucer designed and developed by Kouji Kabuto at NASA, and Earth's first domestically produced UFO. Its shape closely resembles the Adamski-type saucer, the most famous flying saucer design at the time of the show's original broadcast.
It has maneuverability comparable to a Minifor and a top flight speed of Mach 4, and it can operate at considerable altitude within the atmosphere. However, since it was not developed for combat, it carries only light armament, such as small missiles and a machine gun.
Running on photon power, armored in Chogokin Z, and designed by the Kabuto family, it is, in its small way, a direct descendant of Mazinger Z. Even so, whenever it went into battle, it was often outmatched by Saucer Beasts and took considerable damage. Despite its different shape, it may be closer in role to a partner robot like Diana A.""",
        8: """A flying machine developed by Dr. Umon that can be described as an Earth-made Spazer.
Built to support Grendizer's flight capability, it adapts Grendizer for aerial combat when combined (Combination Cross), reaching a top speed of Mach 4.
Its greatest advantage is that the weapons of Grendizer, which are restricted when combined with the original Spazer, can be used to their full potential when combined with the Double Spazer instead. Piloted by Kouji, it also demonstrated high offensive performance even while separated.
All of the Earth-made Spazers run on the same photon quantum energy as Grendizer, but their armor is made of Chogokin New Z.""",
        9: """The second Earth-made Spazer, developed by Dr. Umon to enhance Grendizer's underwater combat capability.
It is a versatile machine capable of operating in both air and water even on its own, reaching a top underwater speed of 40 knots. However, since it can only dive to a depth of 400 meters, Grendizer needed to use a different mecha, the 'Ultra Submarine,' to operate in the deep sea.
Its greatest benefit is that, when combined with Grendizer, it can replenish the photon quantum energy that Grendizer consumes at a sharply increased rate underwater. It was primarily operated by Hikaru, and it contributed greatly to the fight against the Vega Beasts.""",
        10: """The third Earth-made Spazer, built by Dr. Umon to enable Grendizer to fight underground.
It can operate in both air and underground even on its own, reaching a maximum underground speed of Mach 1. Once combined, its arm-mounted weapons become unusable, but its 'Drill Attack,' which uses two large drills capable of effortlessly crushing solid bedrock, is powerful, giving it some of the greatest offensive power among the Earth-made Spazers.
Kouji initially served as its pilot as well, but once Maria appeared, control was entrusted to her.""",
        11: """A medium-sized saucer of the Vega Star Alliance forces.
It is roughly twice the size of the small Minifor saucer, and it is equipped with a Vegatron Beam Cannon.
They swarm Grendizer in a variety of formations, but are usually wiped out in an instant.""",
    },
}
